          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गोधूलि — godhūli — \"dusk (when the cattle come home)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गोधूलि में गायें गाँव लौट रही थीं। godhūli meṁ gāyẽ gā̃v lauṭ rahī thīṁ. At dusk the cows were coming back to the village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गोधूलि (godhūli) is a tatsama, Sanskrit godhūli (Monier-Williams), literally the dust of go, a word for both the cow and the earth. Monier-Williams reads it as earth-dust, the haze that seems to rise at that hour; the usual telling is the dust raised by the cattle coming home. It is still an auspicious time for weddings."
            }
          ]
        },
